WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.004 --> 00:00:02.554
- I'm definitely gonna
get diabetes after this.

00:00:02.554 --> 00:00:06.661
(jazz music)

00:00:06.661 --> 00:00:07.852
- When I think of American cereal

00:00:07.852 --> 00:00:10.917
I just think of sugar. Just plain sugar.

00:00:10.917 --> 00:00:12.146
- I'm so excited to try these,

00:00:12.146 --> 00:00:13.587
I've been waiting years for this.

00:00:13.587 --> 00:00:15.282
- I'm ready.
- Yup, let's do this.

00:00:15.282 --> 00:00:18.028
- Cap'n? What happened to the "tain"?

00:00:18.028 --> 00:00:18.823
Captain.

00:00:18.823 --> 00:00:20.529
- It's cap'n. Cap'n Crunch.

00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:23.693
- Doesn't smell like anything.

00:00:23.693 --> 00:00:25.080
- It's weirdly boring.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:26.891
- It's, like, glazed with sugar,

00:00:26.891 --> 00:00:27.876
which I find is awesome.

00:00:27.876 --> 00:00:29.478
- They really do taste like Cheerios.

00:00:29.478 --> 00:00:30.978
- This kind of reminds me of

00:00:30.978 --> 00:00:32.649
when I was a kid and had Cornflakes,

00:00:32.649 --> 00:00:34.089
you would put the sugar on.

00:00:34.089 --> 00:00:36.551
But with this you need
to take some sugar out.

00:00:38.691 --> 00:00:41.207
This isn't cereal. These are cookies.

00:00:41.927 --> 00:00:43.444
- Why did you give me cookies in a bowl?

00:00:43.444 --> 00:00:44.186
- Not bad.

00:00:44.186 --> 00:00:45.928
- It doesn't really taste
like a cookie, though.

00:00:45.928 --> 00:00:47.043
- This is Nutrigrain but it's got

00:00:47.043 --> 00:00:48.436
chocolate chip cookies in it.

00:00:48.436 --> 00:00:51.594
- No need to give Santa
a big glass of milk

00:00:51.594 --> 00:00:52.755
and a giant cookie.

00:00:52.755 --> 00:00:54.217
Instead just give him a bowl of this.

00:00:54.217 --> 00:00:55.296
- I'm not a fan.

00:00:55.296 --> 00:00:57.621
- See, I think America was
just running out of ideas.

00:00:57.621 --> 00:00:59.386
They just chucked a
bunch of cookies in a box

00:00:59.386 --> 00:01:00.919
and called it cereal.

00:01:00.919 --> 00:01:03.333
- I'm not a big fan of
Reese's peanut butter cups.

00:01:03.333 --> 00:01:04.284
That's too intense.

00:01:04.284 --> 00:01:06.560
- And now it's in a cereal.
- (laughs)

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.209
- These look like giant Coco Puffs.

00:01:08.209 --> 00:01:10.020
- They remind me of pet food.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:11.274
- Or rabbit poo.

00:01:11.274 --> 00:01:14.176
- It tastes so good, but I
think I shouldn't like it.

00:01:14.176 --> 00:01:15.732
- This is like a hollow Kit Kat.

00:01:15.732 --> 00:01:17.497
- I like peanut butter but I don't think

00:01:17.497 --> 00:01:19.099
it belongs in cereal.

00:01:19.099 --> 00:01:20.794
- This is like a sad cereal.

00:01:20.794 --> 00:01:22.837
- I'd probably have this after a breakup.

00:01:22.837 --> 00:01:24.718
- So can I take this box home with me?

00:01:24.718 --> 00:01:26.296
Cause, I'm, I'm done.

00:01:26.296 --> 00:01:27.550
I've never heard of this before.

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.363
What is Cinnamon Toast Crunch?

00:01:29.363 --> 00:01:30.754
- These look like Grain Waves.

00:01:30.754 --> 00:01:32.217
- You can actually smell the cinnamon.

00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:33.494
- Tastes like Christmas.

00:01:33.494 --> 00:01:35.770
- Cinnamon scrolls at
Cole's that you can buy.

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:36.745
- Yeah!
- Yeah.

00:01:36.745 --> 00:01:38.556
- It tastes exactly like cinnamon toast

00:01:38.556 --> 00:01:40.298
which is awesome and
then it's mixed with milk

00:01:40.298 --> 00:01:41.621
and just makes it even better.

00:01:41.621 --> 00:01:43.479
- Mm, so good.

00:01:43.479 --> 00:01:46.311
- I expected doughnuts,
these are not doughnuts.

00:01:46.311 --> 00:01:48.146
- These are better than doughnuts.

00:01:48.146 --> 00:01:49.259
- Now there's something good

00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:50.374
about how simple this is.

00:01:50.374 --> 00:01:51.280
I appreciate that.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:52.534
- I would happily move to America

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:53.950
just for Cinnamon Toast Crunch.

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:55.644
- Trix are for kids.

00:01:55.644 --> 00:01:57.712
- I don't understand why I have a rainbow

00:01:57.712 --> 00:01:58.570
in my bowl.

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:01.333
- All I thought was Nerds in milk.

00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:03.616
- This is like Froot Loops but on crack.

00:02:03.616 --> 00:02:05.630
- Hands down I could
buy this for breakfast.

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:07.488
I could buy this lunch and dinner as well.

00:02:08.268 --> 00:02:09.212
- Would you have this again?

00:02:09.212 --> 00:02:11.783
- Um, no, no, I wouldn't.

00:02:11.783 --> 00:02:12.896
- Mr. Prime Minister?

00:02:12.896 --> 00:02:14.615
Get these on our shelves, right now.

00:02:14.615 --> 00:02:15.846
- Lucky Charms!

00:02:15.846 --> 00:02:17.911
- Is that marshmallow in there?

00:02:17.911 --> 00:02:19.397
- Why do you have
marshmallows in your cereal?

00:02:19.397 --> 00:02:20.767
- Yeah, that's just weird America.

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:22.394
- It's one of those cereals
that you put in the cart

00:02:22.394 --> 00:02:23.671
and your mom says, "Get it out."

00:02:23.671 --> 00:02:24.429
- Yeah.
- (laughs)

00:02:24.429 --> 00:02:26.962
- Oh! It's so slimy, too.
- Oh, no.

00:02:26.962 --> 00:02:29.011
- Yeah, no. I'm good. I'm done.

00:02:29.011 --> 00:02:30.912
- This is more of a
dessert than a breakfast.

00:02:30.912 --> 00:02:32.819
- The marshmallows in the Lucky Charms

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:35.168
are like the Beyonce in Destiny's Child,

00:02:35.168 --> 00:02:37.125
take them away and it's nothing.

00:02:37.125 --> 00:02:38.392
- The cereal isn't the greatest

00:02:38.392 --> 00:02:40.273
but I know it means well because, hey,

00:02:40.273 --> 00:02:42.564
there's rainbows in here
so it's progressive.

00:02:42.564 --> 00:02:44.645
- After today, I think American cereal

00:02:44.645 --> 00:02:46.224
was exactly what I thought it was:

00:02:46.224 --> 00:02:47.989
colorful, sugary, and diabetes.

00:02:47.989 --> 00:02:50.102
- America you've set the
bar for out-there cereals

00:02:50.102 --> 00:02:52.155
and the rest of the world
has a lot to live up to.

00:02:52.155 --> 00:02:53.744
- I'm on the sugar rush
of my life right now

00:02:53.744 --> 00:02:55.097
so, thank you for that, America.

00:02:55.097 --> 00:02:58.337
- I feel as if Australian
cereal is Lil' Wayne

00:02:58.337 --> 00:03:01.234
but American cereal is Jay-Z.

